  "facts": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Garden City was patterned after the 19th‑century English garden city idea, with most homes originally set on one‑acre plots for family gardens.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden_City%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In June 1927, Garden City transitioned from a township area to a village, with Arnold Folker elected its first Village President.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden_City%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Six years later, the village officially became the city of Garden City, marking its rise to municipal status.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden_City%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Garden City hosts the first ever Kmart store, a retail chain that would grow into a national icon.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden_City%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The first Little Caesars pizza restaurant also opened its doors in Garden City, launching a franchise that would become worldwide.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden_City%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "In 1952, Henry Ford’s honeymoon cottage was relocated to Garden City from Dearborn, adding a historic landmark to the town.",
